": "Wiki \u00b7 how a page is stored (proposal)", "radius": 14}, "WkPhoneWeb.dc.html": {"x": 1880, "y": 12340, "w": 390, "h": 844, "title": "Wiki \u00b7 a web page as the source \u2014 a saved copy, with where it came from", "radius": 48, "is_interactive": true}}, "order": ["ChatHome.dc.html", "Main.dc.html", "ChatPermission.dc.html", "ChatQuestion.dc.html", "ChatPlaces.dc.html", "Home.dc.html", "Calendar.dc.html", "Tasks.dc.html", "Wiki.dc.html", "Search.dc.html", "You.dc.html", "Place.dc.html", "DuoFolded.dc.html", "DuoOpen.dc.html", "DesktopChat.dc.html", "LightChatPermission.dc.html", "LightChatQuestion.dc.html", "LightCalendar.dc.html", "LightTasks.dc.html", "LightPlace.dc.html", "LightDuoOpen.dc.html", "ClusterProto.dc.html", "BarRoot.dc.html", "BarCompact.dc.html", "BarSearch.dc.html", "BarCalendar.dc.html", "BarDetail.dc.html", "BarRequest.dc.html", "BarMap.dc.html", "CapsuleProto.dc.html", "CapRoot.dc.html", "CapCompact.dc.html", "CapWiki.dc.html", "CapCalendar.dc.html", "CapDetail.dc.html", "CapRequest.dc.html", "CapMap.dc.html", "RowDuoFolded.dc.html", "RowDuoOpen.dc.html", "RowDuoBloom.dc.html", "RowDuoFocus.dc.html", "RowDesktop.dc.html", "RowDesktopFocus.dc.html", "RowDuoDeeper.dc.html", "RowDesktopDeeper.dc.html", "WikiList.dc.html", "FoldChat.dc.html", "FoldCalendar.dc.html", "FoldTasks.dc.html", "FoldWiki.dc.html", "FoldSearch.dc.html", "FoldYou.dc.html", "FoldPlace.dc.html", "OpenChat.dc.html", "OpenCalendar.dc.html", "OpenTasks.dc.html", "OpenWiki.dc.html", "OpenSearch.dc.html", "OpenYou.dc.html", "OpenPlace.dc.html", "DeskChat.dc.html", "DeskCalendar.dc.html", "DeskTasks.dc.html", "DeskWiki.dc.html", "DeskSearch.dc.html", "DeskYou.dc.html", "DeskPlace.dc.html", "CalPhoneDay.dc.html", "CalPhoneWeek.dc.html", "CalPhoneMonth.dc.html", "CalPhoneEvent.dc.html", "CalLightWeek.dc.html", "CalLightMonth.dc.html", "CalFoldDay.dc.html", "CalFoldWeek.dc.html", "CalFoldMonth.dc.html", "CalOpenDay.dc.html", "CalOpenWeek.dc.html", "CalOpenMonth.dc.html", "CalDeskDay.dc.html", "CalDeskWeek.dc.html", "CalDeskMonth.dc.html", "CalDeskEvent.dc.html", "WkPhone.dc.html", "WkPhoneMid.dc.html", "WkPhoneLow.dc.html", "WkPhoneCite.dc.html", "WkPhoneWeb.dc.html", "WkPhoneQuestion.dc.html", "WkPhoneSources.dc.html", "WkPhoneList.dc.html", "WkLight.dc.html", "WkLightCite.dc.html", "WkOpen.dc.html", "WkOpenCite.dc.html", "WkDesk.dc.html", "WkDeskCite.dc.html", "WkFormat.dc.html"], "notes": {"row1": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Phone \u2014 the agent conversation", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2270}, "row2": {"x": 0, "y": 944, "text": "Phone \u2014 every module", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3210}, "row3": {"x": 0, "y": 2188, "text": "iPhone Duo folded \u2014 the phone layout, wider and shorter", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2956}, "row4": {"x": 0, "y": 6392, "text": "Light mode \u2014 contrast check", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3240}, "cl1": {"x": 0, "y": -300, "text": "Bar (iOS reference) \u2014 tab bar + one accessory", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3680, "page": "cluster"}, "cl2": {"x": 0, "y": 944, "text": "Row \u2014 one structure, three states: row, bloom, focus", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3680, "page": "cluster"}, "clr1": {"x": -560, "y": 0, "w": 460, "page": "cluster", "fill": "blue", "text": "Bar \u2014 six rules\n\n1. The top is for reading: large title, then a small passive title in the top edge. No buttons up there.\n2. Three slots: bar, one accessory, a temporary sheet.\n3. Bar = tab bar + Search circle at a root; one level in it folds into Back + the page's actions.\n4. Accessory = the one input or control the module wants under the thumb. Never a title.\n5. Scroll down or start typing \u2192 the bar folds into a circle and the accessory slides inline: one row.\n6. Requests, questions and place details grow out of the accessory as a sheet, then shrink back into it."}, "clr2": {"x": -560, "y": 1244, "w": 460, "page": "cluster", "fill": "purple", "text": "Row \u2014 [leading circle] [centre] [trailing circle], always.\n\nA page may request:\n\u2022 Field (compose / query / capture) \u2192 centre\n\u2022 Switcher \u2192 centre\n\u2022 Back \u2192 leading circle\n\u2022 Primary \u2192 trailing circle\n\u2022 Actions \u2192 trailing \u2026 circle\n\u2022 Focus card \u2192 the whole cluster\n\nBloom: the circles tilt up into a column above their circle \u2014 the module circle into the modules (and the centre becomes search), \u2026 into the actions. No accent: the current one is a filled circle.\nFocus: a request, question or place takes the whole cluster down to the bottom edge. In chat, picking a question lifts it out of the conversation and leaves an \u201cAnswering below\u201d outline."}, "clr3": {"x": -560, "y": 620, "w": 460, "page": "cluster", "fill": "gray", "text": "Try it: tap \u201cLisbon trip\u201d, then Review or Answer on the agent's cards; tap the module circle or \u2026 to bloom them; tap the Casa Alfama chip for a place. Every change is the same pieces of glass changing shape."}, "cl3": {"x": 0, "y": 2188, "text": "Every size: one bar on the phone, two areas when the screen opens", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 3846, "page": "cluster"}, "clr4": {"x": -560, "y": 2488, "w": 460, "page": "cluster", "fill": "green", "text": "Touch blooms when space is short; otherwise menus lie flat.\n\nPhone and folded Duo: one bar \u2014 [\u2026] [field] [Back / module]. The modules hide behind the module circle and bloom as the bar stood upright; blooming it is search.\n\nDuo open: two bars. Left half: the modules laid flat with their names, plus search. Right half: the open item's bar, its circles gathered in the right thumb's corner \u2014 [field] [\u2026] [Back] \u2014 so nothing waits by the hinge.\n\nDesktop: the open Duo's two bars at desktop size; actions lie flat as icons.\n\nEvery focus card has a way out without answering: a circle at the end of its answer row, right where Back sits in the bar \u2014 \u2715 (Later) on a request or question, \u2039 on a place. Swipe the card down or press Esc for the same.\n\nThe glass stays clear; blue appears only on filled answers inside cards, never on the bar's circles."}, "row5": {"x": 0, "y": 3166, "text": "iPhone Duo open \u2014 list on the left, the open item on the right", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 7600}, "row6": {"x": 0, "y": 4092, "text": "Desktop \u2014 the open Duo, enlarged", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 6000}, "scr1": {"x": -560, "y": 3466, "w": 460, "fill": "green", "text": "Where requests go on a wide screen.\n\nLeft bar: navigation only \u2014 the modules laid flat, plus search (which turns that bar into the search field).\n\nRight bar: everything the module asks for \u2014 its field or switcher, its Primary and actions \u2014 with the circles in the right thumb's corner on the Duo and laid flat as icons on desktop.\n\nThe list in the left half never gets controls of its own. Details that aren't a page (a place, an event) open as a focus card in the right half."}, "calt": {"x": 0, "y": 7492, "text": "Calendar \u2014 Day \u00b7 Week \u00b7 Month at every size", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 6000}, "caln": {"x": -560, "y": 7792, "w": 460, "fill": "green", "text": "All of these are live: switch Day \u00b7 Week \u00b7 Month in the bar, tap a day in the week header or the month to jump to it, tap an event to open it as a focus card (\u2039 closes it).\n\nPhone: Day = week strip + the day's hours; Week = all seven days as narrow columns; Month = dots, with the chosen day's agenda below.\n\nWide: the left half keeps a small month to pick days (or, in Month, the chosen day's agenda); the right half shows the view. Desktop months show event names in the cells.\n\nMulti-day events (Lisbon weekend) run along the all-day row in Day and Week and as a bar under the days in Month."}, "wkt": {"x": 0, "y": 12040, "text": "Wiki \u2014 every statement cites its source", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 6400}, "wkn": {"x": -560, "y": 12340, "w": 460, "fill": "green", "text": "Every sentence carries numbered chips pointing to the original words in a stored source: a conversation with the agent (typed or a transcribed voice note), an imported document or image, or a web page the agent fetched \u2014 always the copy saved at the time, with a link back to where it came from.\n\nTap a chip: the source opens as a focus card with the cited words highlighted; \u2715 returns you to the page.\n\nOnly the agent writes pages \u2014 you steer it in chat. Pages also embed live things from the other modules (a timeline from Calendar, tasks, a place) and keep open questions until you answer them.\n\nStored as structured data, not markdown: see the last board."}}, "designSystems": [{"title": "Smoked Glass", "namespace": "smokedglass", "artifact": "https://claude.ai/artifact/1FrACu1Y3srp8YurTKc1e4", "version": null, "copiedAt": "2026-10-22T19:45:00Z"}]}